            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for suggestion!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce this: with LuaSnip and snippets I have this working as you expect. In particular, I use plain `require('mini.pairs').setup()` and this snippet:\r\n```json\r\n  \"fori\": {\r\n    \"prefix\": \"fori\",\r\n    \"body\": \"for ${1:idx},${2:val} in ipairs(${3:table_name}) do\\n\\t$4\\nend$0\",\r\n    \"description\": \"for .. ipairs()\"\r\n  },\r\n```\r\n\r\nRight after expanding it (with LuaSnip's own `expand_or_jump()` function) I have `idx` selected in Select mode. Pressing single `(` leads to inserting `()` and cursor ending up in between them.\r\n\r\nCouple of questions:\r\n- Do you have pairs set up in Insert mode? What does `imap {` say?\r\n- What does `smap {` and `vmap {` say? Maybe they are somehow remapped in Select mode.\r\n- How do you expand snippet? With plain `LuaSnip` or with 'nvim-cmp'? Does it work if expanded with another method from these two?",
